{* ctools-attribution:begin (generated by scripts/sync_attribution.py; edit config/attribution.json)}{...}
{marker acknowledgments}{...}
{title:Acknowledgments}

{pstd}
{cmd:cegen} reimplements {cmd:egen}, an official Stata command, and the
{cmd:egen} functions that ship with Stata. Its syntax, functions, options,
storage types, labels, and messages follow {cmd:egen}. The {cmd:threads()} and
{cmd:verbose} options are additions in ctools.

{pstd}
{cmd:cegen} is pinned to this version of {cmd:egen}:

{p2colset 9 27 29 2}{...}
{p2col:Command}{cmd:egen} (official Stata){p_end}
{p2col:Authors}StataCorp LLC{p_end}
{p2col:Version}{cmd:egen.ado} 3.4.2{p_end}
{p2col:Date}April 13, 2020{p_end}
{p2col:Header line}{cmd:*! version 3.4.2  13apr2020}{p_end}
{p2col:Shipped with}StataNow 19.5 (revision 14 Oct 2026){p_end}
{p2colreset}{...}

{pstd}
{cmd:cegen} follows {cmd:egen} as it behaves in this Stata release.
{cmd:which egen} shows the version of {cmd:egen.ado} in your Stata.
{help ctools##acknowledgments:help ctools} lists the pinned versions of all
ctools commands.

{pstd}
Please report bugs and questions about {cmd:cegen} at
{browse "https://github.com/mdroste/stata-ctools/issues":github.com/mdroste/stata-ctools/issues}.
StataCorp does not support {cmd:cegen}. Undocumented differences between
{cmd:cegen} and {cmd:egen} are bugs in {cmd:cegen}.

{pstd}
Several {cmd:egen} functions began as contributions by Stata users, and their
files in Stata say so: {cmd:anyvalue()}, {cmd:mad()}, and {cmd:mdev()} are
based on programs by Nicholas J. Cox ({it:Stata Technical Bulletin} 50, insert
dm70), and {cmd:mtr()} is an update of a program by Timothy J. Schmidt
({it:Stata Technical Bulletin} 22, insert sss1.1). The Acknowledgments of [D]
egen in the Stata manuals also credit David Clayton and Michael Hills with
{cmd:cut()} and Nicholas J. Cox with many of the other functions.

{pstd}
{cmd:cegen} does not copy the tax tables of {cmd:mtr()} and does not
reimplement functions that ship outside Stata, such as those of
{cmd:egenmore}: it passes these calls to {cmd:egen} itself.

{pstd}
The original command is described in:

{phang2}Cox, N. J. 1999. dm70: Extensions to generate, extended.
{it:Stata Technical Bulletin} 50: 9-17.{p_end}

{phang2}Schmidt, T. J. 1994. sss1.1: Updated U.S. marginal income tax rate
function. {it:Stata Technical Bulletin} 22: 29.{p_end}
{* ctools-attribution:end}{...}


